# FPGA-Image-Enhancement

## Quantization-Aware Residual CNN for FPGA-Based Image Enhancement

An FPGA-accelerated deep learning pipeline for real-time image enhancement using Residual CNNs, INT8 quantization, and Vitis AI deployment.

This project focuses on building a hardware-efficient image restoration system capable of enhancing degraded images while maintaining high inference speed on FPGA platforms. The deployment pipeline is optimized for low-precision INT8 execution without sacrificing visual restoration quality.

---

# ✨ Highlights

- Residual CNN architecture optimized for image restoration
- INT8 quantization-aware deployment using Vitis AI
- FPGA-accelerated inference with DPU execution
- `.xmodel` generation for Xilinx platforms
- PSNR / SSIM evaluation workflows
- Docker-based reproducible environment
- Hardware vs software benchmarking
- Optimized for edge-AI and embedded deployment

---

# 🚀 Project Overview

Modern image enhancement models often achieve excellent results on GPUs but struggle to run efficiently on edge hardware. This project bridges that gap by combining:

- Deep learning-based image restoration
- FPGA hardware acceleration
- Quantization-aware optimization
- Efficient deployment workflows

The system is designed to restore images affected by:

- Noise
- Blur
- Low-light degradation
- Real-world image artifacts

while achieving fast and efficient inference on FPGA hardware.

---

# 🧠 Deployment Pipeline

```text
Dataset
   ↓
Residual CNN Training
   ↓
Quantization-Aware Optimization
   ↓
INT8 XModel Generation
   ↓
DPU Compilation
   ↓
FPGA Inference
   ↓
Enhanced Output
```

